module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.HighestWeight.Basic
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.UniversalEnveloping.Module

public section

/-!
# Verma modules

Fix a base `b` of the root system of a splitting Cartan subalgebra `H` of a Killing-semisimple Lie
algebra `L`, and a linear form `lam` on `H`. The **Verma module** `M(lam)` is the universal module
carrying a vector on which `H` acts through `lam` and which the positive nilradical `n⁺`
annihilates. It is built here as the quotient

`M(lam) = U(L) / U(L) · ({n⁺} ∪ {h - lam h : h ∈ H})`

of the enveloping algebra by the left ideal generated by the raising operators and by the
`lam`-shifted Cartan, which is the presentation form of the induced module `U(L) ⊗_{U(𝔟)} K_lam`.
Reading that quotient as a Lie module is exactly what
`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asLieRingModule` is for, so no new module structure is built
here beyond the left ideal itself.

The content of the file is the **universal property**: for a Lie module `M` and a vector `v` in it
on which `H` acts through `lam` and which `n⁺` annihilates — in particular a highest weight vector
of weight `lam` — there is a *unique* homomorphism `M(lam) → M` sending the canonical generator to
`v` (`TauCeti.existsUnique_vermaLift`). Existence is the enveloping-algebra dictionary for
homomorphisms applied to `u ↦ u • v`, which kills the defining relations precisely because `v`
satisfies them; uniqueness is that the canonical generator generates `M(lam)`.

## The nonvanishing of `M(lam)`

Every statement in this file is unconditional. Two nonvanishing results hold at this generality:
the canonical generator of `M(lam)` is nonzero as soon as *some* Lie module carries a highest
weight vector of weight `lam` (`TauCeti.vermaGen_ne_zero_of_isHighestWeightVector`, a consequence
of the universal property), and `M(0)` is nonzero outright
(`TauCeti.vermaGen_zero_ne_zero`), the trivial module supplying the vector; so the canonical
generator of `M(0)` is a genuine `TauCeti.IsHighestWeightVector`
(`TauCeti.isHighestWeightVector_vermaGen_zero`).

Nonvanishing for an *arbitrary* `lam` is a much larger statement: it is the
Poincaré--Birkhoff--Witt theorem that `U(L)` is free over `U(n⁻)`, whose injectivity half is open
in `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/UniversalEnveloping/PBW/AssociatedGraded.lean` and which the roadmap stages
as a sub-project of its own. Nothing here assumes it, bundles it as a hypothesis or stands in for
it; the file simply does not state it.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.vermaRelations`: the defining relations, the raising operators together with the
  `lam`-shifted Cartan elements.
* `TauCeti.vermaIdeal`: the left ideal of `U(L)` they generate.
* `TauCeti.vermaModule`: the Verma module `M(lam)`, with its `U(L)`-module, `K`-module and Lie
  module structures.
* `TauCeti.vermaMk`: the quotient map `U(L) → M(lam)`, as a `U(L)`-linear map.
* `TauCeti.vermaGen`: the canonical generator, the class of `1`.
* `TauCeti.vermaLift`: the homomorphism out of `M(lam)` classified by a vector satisfying the
  defining relations, and `TauCeti.vermaLiftₗ`, its `U(L)`-linear shadow.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.lie_vermaGen_of_mem_positiveNilradical` and `TauCeti.lie_vermaGen`: the canonical
  generator is annihilated by `n⁺`, and `H` acts on it through `lam`.
* `TauCeti.span_vermaGen` and `TauCeti.lieSpan_vermaGen`: the canonical generator generates
  `M(lam)`, over `U(L)` and as a Lie module.
* `TauCeti.existsUnique_vermaLift`: **the universal property of the Verma module.**
* `TauCeti.range_vermaLift`: the image of the classifying map is the submodule generated by the
  vector it was built from, so every highest weight module of weight `lam` is a quotient of
  `M(lam)`.
* `TauCeti.vermaGen_ne_zero_of_isHighestWeightVector`: the canonical generator is nonzero as soon
  as some Lie module carries a highest weight vector of weight `lam`.
* `TauCeti.vermaGen_zero_ne_zero` and `TauCeti.isHighestWeightVector_vermaGen_zero`: `M(0)` is
  nonzero, and its canonical generator is a highest weight vector of weight `0`.
* `TauCeti.vermaGen_eq_zero_iff`: the canonical generator vanishes exactly when the defining left
  ideal is improper.

## Implementation notes

The relations are taken in the form `ι x` for `x ∈ n⁺` and `ι h - lam h` for `h ∈ H`, with `ι` the
canonical Lie map into `U(L)`; the Borel `𝔟 = H ⊕ n⁺` therefore enters only through its two
summands, which is what makes the relation set easy to check against. Since `n⁺` and `H` together
span `𝔟` (`TauCeti.borelSubalgebra_toSubmodule`), the ideal is the one the tensor description names,
but no such comparison is needed for anything below and none is asserted.

`vermaModule` is a `def` rather than an abbreviation for the quotient, as the roadmap pins it, and
carries its instances explicitly. Everything downstream goes through `TauCeti.vermaMk` and the
lemmas about it, never through the quotient presentation.

The universal property is stated as an `ExistsUnique` over Lie module homomorphisms, evaluated at
the canonical generator. The alternative phrasing "every highest weight vector of weight `lam`
receives a map from `M(lam)`" is weaker, since the zero map satisfies it; evaluation at the
generator is what pins the map down.

The roadmap pins the universal property against `TauCeti.IsHighestWeightVector`. It is stated here
against the two relations such a vector satisfies instead, since neither the construction of the
classifying map nor its uniqueness uses `TauCeti.IsHighestWeightVector.ne_zero`, and requiring
`v ≠ 0` would exclude the classifying map of the zero vector. The pinned form is the immediate
specialization
`existsUnique_vermaLift hv.lie_eq_smul fun x hx => hv.lie_eq_zero_of_mem_positiveNilradical hx`,
so no separate restatement is kept.

The canonical generator is called `TauCeti.vermaGen`, not `vermaHighestWeightVector`: for a general
`lam` it is not known to be a highest weight vector until the Poincaré--Birkhoff--Witt input above
lands, and a name asserting that it is would be a claim this file does not prove. The universal
property carries the `existsUnique_` prefix its statement shape asks for, as elsewhere in this
library.

## References

* J. E. Humphreys, *Introduction to Lie Algebras and Representation Theory*, GTM 9, Ch. VI, §20.
* N. Bourbaki, *Lie Groups and Lie Algebras*, Chapter VII, §1.

This builds the `vermaModule` and `vermaModule_universal` targets of Layer 3, "highest weight
vectors, Verma modules, and `L(λ)`", of
`TauCetiRoadmap/RepresentationTheory/LieHighestWeight/README.md`, the layer that
`TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/UniversalEnveloping/Module.lean` names as the consumer of its converse
translation `asLieRingModule`. That layer's `isHighestWeightVector_vermaHighestWeightVector` is
reached here for `lam = 0`, as `TauCeti.isHighestWeightVector_vermaGen_zero`; for a general `lam`
it waits on the Poincaré--Birkhoff--Witt sub-project.
-/

namespace TauCeti

open LieAlgebra LieModule Module

universe u v w

variable {K : Type u} {L : Type v} [Field K] [CharZero K] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]
  [IsKilling K L] [FiniteDimensional K L]
  {H : LieSubalgebra K L} [H.IsCartanSubalgebra] [IsTriangularizable K H L]
  (b : (IsKilling.rootSystem H).Base) (lam : Dual K H)

/-! ### The defining left ideal -/

/-- The **defining relations of the Verma module** `M(lam)`: the raising operators `ι x` for `x` in
the positive nilradical, together with the `lam`-shifted Cartan elements `ι h - lam h`. -/
def vermaRelations : Set (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :=
  {u | ∃ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, u = UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K x} ∪
    {u | ∃ h : H, u = UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (h : L) -
      algebraMap K (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (lam h)}

/-- The **defining left ideal of the Verma module** `M(lam)`, generated by
`TauCeti.vermaRelations`. -/
def vermaIdeal :
    Submodule (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :=
  Submodule.span (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (vermaRelations b lam)

variable {b lam}

/-- A raising operator lies in the defining left ideal. -/
theorem ι_mem_vermaIdeal {x : L} (hx : x ∈ positiveNilradical H b) :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K x ∈ vermaIdeal b lam :=
  Submodule.subset_span (Or.inl ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩)

/-- A `lam`-shifted Cartan element lies in the defining left ideal. -/
theorem ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_vermaIdeal (h : H) :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (h : L) -
        algebraMap K (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (lam h) ∈ vermaIdeal b lam :=
  Submodule.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨h, rfl⟩)

variable (b lam)

/-! ### The Verma module and its structures -/

/-- **The Verma module** `M(lam) = U(L) / U(L) · (n⁺ + (H - lam))`, the universal module generated
by a vector on which the Cartan subalgebra acts through `lam` and which the positive nilradical
annihilates. -/
def vermaModule : Type (max u v) :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L ⧸ vermaIdeal b lam

noncomputable instance : AddCommGroup (vermaModule b lam) :=
  inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L ⧸ vermaIdeal b lam))

noncomputable instance : Module (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (vermaModule b lam) :=
  inferInstanceAs
    (Module (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L)
      (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L ⧸ vermaIdeal b lam))

noncomputable instance : Module K (vermaModule b lam) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module K (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L ⧸ vermaIdeal b lam))

instance : IsScalarTower K (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (vermaModule b lam) :=
  inferInstanceAs
    (IsScalarTower K (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L)
      (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L ⧸ vermaIdeal b lam))

noncomputable instance : LieRingModule L (vermaModule b lam) :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asLieRingModule K L (vermaModule b lam)

noncomputable instance : LieModule K L (vermaModule b lam) :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asLieModule K L (vermaModule b lam)

/-- The compatibility of the `U(L)`-action on the Verma module with its Lie bracket, in the form the
enveloping-algebra dictionary of `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/UniversalEnveloping/Module.lean` consumes. -/
theorem ι_smul_vermaModule (x : L) (m : vermaModule b lam) :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K x • m = ⁅x, m⁆ :=
  (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asLieRingModule_bracket K L (vermaModule b lam) x m).symm

/-- **The quotient map** `U(L) → M(lam)`, as a `U(L)`-linear map. -/
def vermaMk :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L →ₗ[UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L] vermaModule b lam :=
  (vermaIdeal b lam).mkQ

/-- The quotient map onto the Verma module is surjective. -/
theorem vermaMk_surjective : Function.Surjective (vermaMk b lam) :=
  Submodule.mkQ_surjective _

variable {b lam}

/-- An element of `U(L)` has zero class in the Verma module exactly when it lies in the defining
left ideal. -/
@[simp]
theorem vermaMk_eq_zero_iff {u : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L} :
    vermaMk b lam u = 0 ↔ u ∈ vermaIdeal b lam :=
  Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _

/-- The quotient map is `U(L)`-linear, so it turns left multiplication into the action. -/
theorem vermaMk_smul (u v : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :
    vermaMk b lam (u * v) = u • vermaMk b lam v :=
  map_smul (vermaMk b lam) u v

/-- The Lie action on the Verma module is left multiplication in `U(L)`. -/
theorem lie_vermaMk (x : L) (u : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :
    ⁅x, vermaMk b lam u⁆ = vermaMk b lam (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K x * u) := by
  rw [vermaMk_smul, ι_smul_vermaModule]

/-- The quotient map is `K`-linear. -/
theorem vermaMk_smul_scalar (c : K) (u : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :
    vermaMk b lam (c • u) = c • vermaMk b lam u :=
  (Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul _ c u)

variable (b lam)

/-- **The canonical generator** of the Verma module, the class of `1`. -/
noncomputable def vermaGen : vermaModule b lam :=
  vermaMk b lam 1

/-- Every element of the Verma module is a multiple of the canonical generator. -/
theorem vermaMk_eq_smul_vermaGen (u : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :
    vermaMk b lam u = u • vermaGen b lam := by
  rw [vermaGen, ← vermaMk_smul, mul_one]

/-- **The canonical generator generates the Verma module** as a `U(L)`-module. -/
theorem span_vermaGen :
    Submodule.span (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) {vermaGen b lam} = ⊤ := by
  refine Submodule.eq_top_iff'.2 fun m => ?_
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := vermaMk_surjective b lam m
  rw [vermaMk_eq_smul_vermaGen]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ u (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _)

variable {b lam}

/-- The canonical generator is annihilated by the positive nilradical. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_vermaGen_of_mem_positiveNilradical {x : L} (hx : x ∈ positiveNilradical H b) :
    ⁅x, vermaGen b lam⁆ = 0 := by
  rw [vermaGen, lie_vermaMk, mul_one, vermaMk_eq_zero_iff]
  exact ι_mem_vermaIdeal hx

/-- The Cartan subalgebra acts on the canonical generator through `lam`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_vermaGen (h : H) : ⁅(h : L), vermaGen b lam⁆ = lam h • vermaGen b lam := by
  have hmem := ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_vermaIdeal (lam := lam) (b := b) h
  rw [← vermaMk_eq_zero_iff (b := b) (lam := lam), map_sub, sub_eq_zero] at hmem
  rw [vermaGen, lie_vermaMk, mul_one, hmem, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, vermaMk_smul_scalar]

/-- **The canonical generator generates the Verma module** as a Lie module. -/
theorem lieSpan_vermaGen : LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {vermaGen b lam} = ⊤ := by
  refine (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lieSubmoduleOrderIso
    (ι_smul_vermaModule b lam)).injective ?_
  rw [UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lieSubmoduleOrderIso_lieSpan, span_vermaGen, OrderIso.map_top]

/-! ### The universal property -/

section Universal

variable {M : Type w} [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M] [LieRingModule L M] [LieModule K L M]

attribute [local instance] UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.isScalarTower_asModule

variable {v : M}

/-- The relations defining the Verma module annihilate any vector on which the Cartan subalgebra
acts through `lam` and which the positive nilradical annihilates; this is the step that makes the
classifying map below well defined. -/
private theorem vermaIdeal_le_ker_toSpanSingleton
    (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0) :
    vermaIdeal b lam ≤
      LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) M v) := by
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro u (⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ | ⟨h, rfl⟩)
  · simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply,
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule_ι_smul]
    exact hpos x hx
  · simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply, sub_smul,
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule_ι_smul, algebraMap_smul]
    rw [hcartan h, sub_self]

/-- The `U(L)`-linear map out of the Verma module classified by a vector satisfying the defining
relations; the Lie module homomorphism `TauCeti.vermaLift` is its image under the
enveloping-algebra dictionary. -/
noncomputable def vermaLiftₗ (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0) :
    vermaModule b lam →ₗ[UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L] M :=
  (vermaIdeal b lam).liftQ (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) M v)
    (vermaIdeal_le_ker_toSpanSingleton hcartan hpos)

/-- The `U(L)`-linear classifying map sends the class of `u` to `u • v`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vermaLiftₗ_vermaMk (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0)
    (u : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :
    vermaLiftₗ hcartan hpos (vermaMk b lam u) = u • v :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The homomorphism out of the Verma module classified by a vector satisfying the defining
relations**: the unique Lie module homomorphism `M(lam) → M` carrying the canonical generator to
`v`. -/
noncomputable def vermaLift (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0) :
    vermaModule b lam →ₗ⁅K,L⁆ M :=
  (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lieModuleHomEquiv (ι_smul_vermaModule b lam)
      (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule_ι_smul K L M)).symm (vermaLiftₗ hcartan hpos)

/-- The classifying map sends the class of `u` to `u • v`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vermaLift_vermaMk (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0)
    (u : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) :
    vermaLift hcartan hpos (vermaMk b lam u) = u • v := by
  rw [vermaLift, UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.coe_lieModuleHomEquiv_symm]
  exact vermaLiftₗ_vermaMk hcartan hpos u

/-- The classifying map sends the canonical generator to the vector it was built from. -/
@[simp]
theorem vermaLift_vermaGen (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0) :
    vermaLift hcartan hpos (vermaGen b lam) = v := by
  rw [vermaGen, vermaLift_vermaMk, one_smul]

/-- **The universal property of the Verma module.** A vector on which the Cartan subalgebra acts
through `lam` and which the positive nilradical annihilates — in particular a highest weight vector
of weight `lam` — is the image of the canonical generator under exactly one homomorphism
`M(lam) → M`. -/
theorem existsUnique_vermaLift (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0) :
    ∃! φ : vermaModule b lam →ₗ⁅K,L⁆ M, φ (vermaGen b lam) = v := by
  refine ⟨vermaLift hcartan hpos, vermaLift_vermaGen hcartan hpos, fun φ hφ => ?_⟩
  refine DFunLike.coe_injective ?_
  have key := LinearMap.ext_on (R := UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (span_vermaGen b lam)
    (f := UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lieModuleHomEquiv (ι_smul_vermaModule b lam)
      (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule_ι_smul K L M) φ)
    (g := UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lieModuleHomEquiv (ι_smul_vermaModule b lam)
      (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule_ι_smul K L M) (vermaLift hcartan hpos))
    (by
      rintro x rfl
      simpa only [UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.coe_lieModuleHomEquiv] using
        hφ.trans (vermaLift_vermaGen hcartan hpos).symm)
  simpa only [UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.coe_lieModuleHomEquiv] using
    congrArg (fun f : vermaModule b lam →ₗ[UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L] M => ⇑f) key

/-- **Every highest weight module of weight `lam` is a quotient of `M(lam)`**: the image of the
classifying map is the Lie submodule generated by the vector it was built from. -/
theorem range_vermaLift (hcartan : ∀ x : H, ⁅(x : L), v⁆ = lam x • v)
    (hpos : ∀ x ∈ positiveNilradical H b, ⁅x, v⁆ = 0) :
    LieModuleHom.range (vermaLift hcartan hpos) = LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L {v} := by
  have hv' : v ∈ LieSubmodule.lieSpan K L ({v} : Set M) :=
    LieSubmodule.subset_lieSpan (Set.mem_singleton v)
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (LieSubmodule.lieSpan_le.2 (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 ?_))
  · rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := vermaMk_surjective b lam m
    rw [vermaLift_vermaMk]
    refine (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.mem_lieSubmoduleOrderIso
      (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.asModule_ι_smul K L M)).1 ?_
    rw [UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lieSubmoduleOrderIso_lieSpan]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ u (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self v)
  · exact ⟨vermaGen b lam, vermaLift_vermaGen hcartan hpos⟩

end Universal

/-! ### Nonvanishing -/

/-- If some Lie module carries a highest weight vector of weight `lam`, the canonical generator of
`M(lam)` is nonzero: it maps to that vector. -/
theorem vermaGen_ne_zero_of_isHighestWeightVector {M : Type w} [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M]
    [LieRingModule L M] [LieModule K L M] {v : M} (hv : IsHighestWeightVector b lam v) :
    vermaGen b lam ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  apply hv.ne_zero
  rw [← vermaLift_vermaGen hv.lie_eq_smul
    fun x hx => hv.lie_eq_zero_of_mem_positiveNilradical hx, h, map_zero]

/-- **The Verma module of weight `0` is nonzero**: the trivial one-dimensional module carries a
highest weight vector of weight `0`, so the defining left ideal of `M(0)` is proper. -/
theorem vermaGen_zero_ne_zero : vermaGen b (0 : Dual K H) ≠ 0 := by
  refine vermaGen_ne_zero_of_isHighestWeightVector (M := TrivialLieModule K L K)
    (v := (TrivialLieModule.equiv K L K).symm 1) (isHighestWeightVector_iff.2 ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩)
  · exact fun h => one_ne_zero ((TrivialLieModule.equiv K L K).symm.map_eq_zero_iff.1 h)
  · intro x
    rw [trivial_lie_zero]
    simp
  · exact fun x _ => trivial_lie_zero L _ x _

/-- **The canonical generator of `M(0)` is a highest weight vector of weight `0`**, so `M(0)` is a
highest weight module. -/
theorem isHighestWeightVector_vermaGen_zero :
    IsHighestWeightVector b (0 : Dual K H) (vermaGen b 0) :=
  isHighestWeightVector_iff.2 ⟨vermaGen_zero_ne_zero, fun x => lie_vermaGen x,
    fun _ hx => lie_vermaGen_of_mem_positiveNilradical hx⟩

/-- The canonical generator vanishes exactly when the defining left ideal is the whole of `U(L)`. -/
theorem vermaGen_eq_zero_iff : vermaGen b lam = 0 ↔ vermaIdeal b lam = ⊤ := by
  rw [vermaGen, vermaMk_eq_zero_iff]
  refine ⟨fun h => Submodule.eq_top_iff'.2 fun u => ?_, fun h => h ▸ Submodule.mem_top⟩
  simpa only [smul_eq_mul, mul_one] using (vermaIdeal b lam).smul_mem u h

end TauCeti
